            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of muscle spasms with oral dantrolene sodium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>268-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of severe muscle spasms relieved by oral administration of dantrolene sodium is presented. The patient had undergone full-mouth extraction 2 days prior to onset of her spasms. The treatment consisted of intravenous diazepam followed by oral dantrolene sodium. The spasms lasted for approximately 10 days.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
